# Wave W17-U (Route 201): candor turf — lake-shore first meadow: a fresh spring green with pale shore flecks standing in it where Lake Candor’s light comes off the water on the route’s north side (design: calm speckled grass, a lake glinting off its north side; the shipped shore water stands byte-preserved beside it). Route 201’s own ground — the freshest green in Borea: split from Route 101’s camp-meadow turf (Maris) by the shore flecks and the lighter register (lake light vs field camp), and from Route 202’s bed-flecked approach meadow by the missing petals.
